                "text": "I'm testing whether it's simply the highest count of 6s that gets filled, but that doesn't match - in example 1 cells with counts of 3 and 2 both got filled while a count of 1 didn't, yet in the query only the highest count cell got filled despite another cell having 2. The pattern isn't a simple max-count rule, so I need to reconsider the threshold.\n\nNow I'm checking if the rule involves adjacency between the 6s within each cell instead: in example 1, the filled cells had 6s positioned adjacent to each other, while the unfilled single-6 cell obviously couldn't have adjacent pairs. Testing this against the query, cells with adjacent 6 pairs get filled while cells with non-adjacent or single 6s don't - this seems to be the actual rule.",
